  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Frankfort Heights grew around a fort built in 1811, named “Frank’s Fort” after early settler Francis Jordan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Frankfort%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Franklin County, where the city sits, was founded in 1818 as a frontier outpost poised to witness the nation’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklincountyil.gov/county-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When railroad tracks linking Chicago, Paducah, and Memphis were laid just west of Frankfort, many businesses and residents moved to the new commercial center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Frankfort%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coal mining has shaped the region, with mines creating thousands of jobs and funding schools, roads, and other public works.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklincountyil.gov/county-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rend Lake, built under the 1962 Flood Control Act, now provides recreation and water resources for the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklincountyil.gov/county-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Frankfort Area Historical Museum, housed in a renovated three‑story Logan Grade School, preserves the city’s rich past.",
